.TH "MOUSEEVENT.LAYERX" "3JS" "September 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MouseEvent.layerX \- MouseEvent: layerX property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]MouseEvent.layerX\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property returns
the horizontal coordinate of the event relative to the current layer.
.PP
This property takes scrolling of the page into account and returns a
value relative to the whole of the document unless the event occurs
inside a positioned element, where the returned value is relative to the
top left of the positioned element.
.SH VALUE
An integer value in pixels for the x\-coordinate of the mouse pointer,
when the mouse event fired.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]p\f[R]>To display the mouse coordinates please click anywhere on the page.</\f[B]p\f[R]>

<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqd1\(dq>
  <\f[B]span\f[R]>
    This is an un\-positioned div so clicking it will return layerX/layerY values
    almost the same as pageX/PageY values.
  </\f[B]span\f[R]>
</\f[B]div\f[R]>

<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqd2\(dq>
  <\f[B]span\f[R]>
    This is a positioned div so clicking it will return layerX/layerY values
    that are relative to the top\-left corner of this positioned element. Note
    the pageX\(rspageY properties still return the absolute position in the
    document, including page scrolling.
  </\f[B]span\f[R]>

  <\f[B]span\f[R]>
    Make the page scroll more! This is a positioned div so clicking it will
    return layerX/layerY values that are relative to the top\-left corner of this
    positioned element. Note the pageX\(rspageY properties still return the
    absolute position in the document, including page scrolling.
  </\f[B]span\f[R]>
</\f[B]div\f[R]>

<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqd3\(dq>
  <\f[B]form\f[R] name=\(dqform_coords\(dq id=\(dqform1\(dq>
    Parent Element id: <\f[B]input\f[R] type=\(dqtext\(dq name=\(dqparentId\(dq size=\(dq7\(dq /><\f[B]br\f[R] />
    pageX: <\f[B]input\f[R] type=\(dqtext\(dq name=\(dqpageXCoords\(dq size=\(dq7\(dq /> pageY:
    <\f[B]input\f[R] type=\(dqtext\(dq name=\(dqpageYCoords\(dq size=\(dq7\(dq /><\f[B]br\f[R] />
    layerX: <\f[B]input\f[R] type=\(dqtext\(dq name=\(dqlayerXCoords\(dq size=\(dq7\(dq /> layerY:
    <\f[B]input\f[R] type=\(dqtext\(dq name=\(dqlayerYCoords\(dq size=\(dq7\(dq />
  </\f[B]form\f[R]>
</\f[B]div\f[R]>
.EE
.IP
.EX
d1 {
  \f[B]border\f[R]: solid blue 1px;
  \f[B]padding\f[R]: 20px;
}

d2 {
  \f[B]position\f[R]: absolute;
  \f[B]top\f[R]: 180px;
  \f[B]left\f[R]: 80%;
  \f[B]right\f[R]: auto;
  \f[B]width\f[R]: 40%;
  \f[B]border\f[R]: solid blue 1px;
  \f[B]padding\f[R]: 20px;
}

d3 {
  \f[B]position\f[R]: absolute;
  \f[B]top\f[R]: 240px;
  \f[B]left\f[R]: 20%;
  \f[B]width\f[R]: 50%;
  \f[B]border\f[R]: solid blue 1px;
  \f[B]padding\f[R]: 10px;
}
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]function\f[R] showCoords(evt) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] form = document.forms.form_coords;
  \f[B]const\f[R] parentId = evt.target.parentNode.id;
  form.parentId.value = parentId;
  form.pageXCoords.value = evt.pageX;
  form.pageYCoords.value = evt.pageY;
  form.layerXCoords.value = evt.layerX;
  form.layerYCoords.value = evt.layerY;
}

window.addEventListener(\(dqmousedown\(dq, showCoords);
.EE
